#: Game/Levels/Inter/L05subint.lean:39
msgid ""
"**The proof, written out.**\n"
"\n"
"> Suppose §0 and §1, and let §2 be an arbitrary element of §3.  Since §4,\n"
"> §5, and since §6, §7.  Therefore §8.  Since §9 was arbitrary,\n"
"> §10.\n"
"\n"
"To prove an \"and\" statement, you prove each half; that is what §11 set up.\n"
"\n"
"In general, if you think that some theorem §12 could be used to prove the goal, the tactic\n"
"§13 will work backwards from the goal, setting as new goals any hypotheses that are\n"
"needed for the application of the theorem §14.\n"
"\n"
"If your goal has the form §15, then the §16 tactic will have the same\n"
"effect as §17; that is, it will set §18 and §19 as goals to be proven."
msgstr ""
"**La demostración, por escrito.**\n"
"\n"
"> Supongamos que §0 y §1, y sea §2 un elemento arbitrario de §3.  Como §4,\n"
"> §5, y como §6, §7.  Por tanto, §8.  Como §9 era arbitrario,\n"
"> §10.\n"
"\n"
"Para demostrar un enunciado \"y\", demuestras cada mitad; eso es lo que preparó §11.\n"
"\n"
"En general, si crees que algún teorema §12 podría usarse para probar el objetivo, la táctica\n"
"§13 funcionará hacia atrás desde el objetivo, estableciendo como nuevos objetivos las hipótesis que sean necesarias para la aplicación del teorema §14.\n"
"\n"
"Si tu objetivo tiene la forma §15, entonces la táctica §16 tendrá el mismo efecto que §17; es decir, establecerá §18 y §19 como objetivos para ser probados."

