#: Game/Levels/Union/L03cases.lean:52
msgid ""
"**The proof, written out.**\n"
"\n"
"> Suppose §0 and §1, and let §2 be an arbitrary element of §3.  Then either\n"
"> §4 or §5.\n"
">\n"
"> *Case 1:* §6.  Since §7, §8.\n"
">\n"
"> *Case 2:* §9.  Since §10, §11.\n"
">\n"
"> In either case §12.  Since §13 was arbitrary, §14.\n"
"\n"
"§15 is the sentence \"Then either §16 or §17\", and each goal it\n"
"creates is one of the cases.\n"
"\n"
"Note that Lean also has a §18 tactic, but the syntax is a little more complicated.\n"
"That's why we have chosen to use the §19 tactic.\n"
"\n"
"The §20 tactic has other uses.  However, in this game we will be using it only with\n"
"assumptions that are \"or\" statements, to break the proof into cases."
msgstr ""
"**La demostración, por escrito.**\n"
"\n"
"> Supongamos que §0 y §1, y sea §2 un elemento arbitrario de §3.  Entonces\n"
"> §4 o §5.\n"
">\n"
"> *Caso 1:* §6.  Como §7, §8.\n"
">\n"
"> *Caso 2:* §9.  Como §10, §11.\n"
">\n"
"> En cualquier caso, §12.  Como §13 era arbitrario, §14.\n"
"\n"
"§15 es la frase \"Entonces §16 o §17\", y cada objetivo que\n"
"crea es uno de los casos.\n"
"\n"
"Ten en cuenta que Lean también tiene una táctica §18, pero la sintaxis es un poco más complicada. Por eso hemos decidido utilizar la táctica §19.\n"
"\n"
"La táctica §20 tiene otros usos, pero en este juego solo lo utilizaremos con\n"
"hipótesis de tipo \"o\", para dividir la prueba en casos."

