#. §8: `apply And.intro`
#. §9: `And.intro`
#. §10: `«{x}» ∈ B`
#. §11: `«{x}» ∈ C`
#: Game/Levels/Inter/L05subint.lean:23
msgid ""
"If you had §0 and §1, then §2\n"
"would prove the goal.  So there are two ways to proceed.  One possibility is to use\n"
"§3 to introduce the assumptions §4 and §5--that is, if you can see\n"
"how to justify those statements!  Then you can use §6 to prove the goal.\n"
"\n"
"The second possibility is to use the §7 tactic.  If you write\n"
"§8, then Lean will figure out that the\n"
"theorem §9 could be applied to prove the goal, if only you had proofs of\n"
"§10 and §11.  So it will set those two statements as goals, to be proven\n"
"one after the other."
msgstr ""
"Si tuvieras §0 y §1, entonces §2\n"
"probaría el objetivo. Así que hay dos maneras de proceder. Una posibilidad es usar\n"
"§3 para introducir las suposiciones §4 y §5 (¡si es que ves\n"
"cómo justificar esas afirmaciones!). Luego puedes usar §6 para probar el objetivo.\n"
"\n"
"La segunda posibilidad es usar la táctica §7. Si escribes\n"
"§8, entonces Lean se dará cuenta de que el\n"
"teorema §9 podría aplicarse para probar el objetivo, si tan solo tuvieras pruebas de\n"
"§10 y §11. Así que establecerá esas dos afirmaciones como objetivos, para probarlas\n"
"una tras otra."

