msgstr ""
"Juego de Teoría de Conjuntos\n"
"\n"

#: Game/Levels/FamUnion/L07eltwiseinter.lean:82
msgid ""
"Set-builder notation lets you describe a family of sets by a property of its elements.  You'll\n"
"see it again in Family Combination World."
msgstr ""
"La notación de construcción de conjuntos te permite describir una familia de conjuntos mediante una propiedad de sus\n"
"elementos. La volverás a ver en el Mundo de las combinaciones de familias."

#. §0: `x ∈ A → x ∈ C`
#. §1: `x ∈ A`
#. §2: `h3`
#. §3: `intro h3`
#: Game/Levels/Subset/L04imp.lean:61
msgid ""
"Since our goal in this level is the statement §0, our first step for\n"
"this proof is to assume §1.  To introduce that assumption,\n"
"assigning it the identifier §2, type §3."
msgstr ""
"Como nuestro objetivo es §0, el primer paso es asumir §1. Para introducir\n"
"  esta hipótesis asignándole el identificador §2, teclea §3."

#. §0: `x`
#. §1: `x ∈ A ∩ B`
#: Game/Levels/Inter/L03inter_sub_left.lean:20
msgid ""
"Since the goal is a subset statement, you should start by\n"
"introducing an object §0 and the assumption that §1."
msgstr "Como el objetivo es un enunciado de contenido, debes empezar introduciendoun objeto §0 y la hipótesis de que §1."

#. §0: `h1 : A ∈ F`
#. §1: `«{h2A}»`
#. §2: `h1`
#. §3: `«{x}» ∈ A`
#. §4: `«{h2A}» h1`
#: Game/Levels/FamInter/L01intersub.lean:85
msgid ""
"Since we also have §0, you can apply §1 to §2 to prove that §3.\n"
"This means that §4 is a proof of the goal."
msgstr "Como también tenemos §0, puedes aplicar §1 a §2 para probar que §3. Esto significa que §4 es una prueba del objetivo."

#. §0: `apply Iff.intro`
#: Game/Levels/Inter/L08inter_assoc.lean:51
msgid ""
"Since your goal is an \"if and only if\" statement, a good next step\n"
"is §0."
msgstr "Dado que tu objetivo es un enunciado \"si y solo si\", un buen siguientepaso es §0."

#. §0: `intro h1`
#: Game/Levels/Inter/L08inter_assoc.lean:54
msgid ""
"Since your goal is an \"if-then\" statement, a good next step\n"
"is §0."
msgstr " Como tu objetivo es un enunciado  de tipo \"si-entonces\", un buen siguiente paso es §0."

#. §0: `∅`
#. §1: `∅`
#. §2: `A`
#: Game/Levels/Comp/L06emptysub.lean:64
msgid ""
"Since §0 has no elements, the statement \"every element of §1 is an element of §2\" can't\n"
"fail.  Mathematicians say that a statement like this is *vacuously true*."
msgstr ""
"Como §0 no tiene elementos, la afirmación \"todo elemento de §1 es un elemento de §2\" no puede\n"
"fallar. Los matemáticos dicen que una afirmación así es *vacuamente verdadera*."

#. §0: `«{h1}»`
#. §1: `«{h1}» _`
#. §2: `False`
#. §3: `«{x}» ∈ ⋃₀ F`
#. §4: `apply «{h1}»`
#. §5: `«{x}» ∈ ⋃₀ F`
#: Game/Levels/FamCombo/L01compunion.lean:38
msgid ""
"Since §0 is a negative statement, a good way to reach a contradiction\n"
"would be to contradict it.  In other words, §1 would prove the goal §2 if you can\n"
"fill in the blank with a proof of §3.  That means the tactic §4 will\n"
